{block name="title}murder motel{/block}
{block name="content"}
<div class="blurb vstretch">
<div class="body">
<ul>
<li><strong>What it is</strong>
<ul>
<li>A multiplayer BBS door game where players hunt each other through a 140-room motel</li>
<li>Each player gets assigned a target to eliminate - kill them and you get a new one</li>
<li>Last one standing wins (though the dead can revive, so that's rare)</li>
<li>Inspired by the movies <em>Clue</em> and <em>Friday the 13th</em></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>How to play</strong>
<ul>
<li>Enter the motel and you're automatically registered</li>
<li>Collect weapon parts scattered around - 2 pieces make a weapon</li>
<li>Find your target and KILL them before they kill you</li>
<li>Max 60 moves per call, up to 30 players at once - check STATUS to see your target</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>History</strong>
<ul>
<li>Classic Commodore 64 door game, later ported to Color64, Image BBS 1.X and 3.0</li>
<li>Original by Mark Dickinson, adapted by Brent Hendricks (Rug Rat)</li>
<li>Now rebuilt from the ground up for bbsengine6 - objects and NPCs stored in the database for extensibility</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Technical</strong>
<ul>
<li>Runs as a bbsengine6 module</li>
<li>5 floors: 4 above ground plus extensive basement</li>
<li>Object-oriented: Living base class with Player and NPC subclasses (the thief and wolf are NPCs)</li>
<li>All objects have a <code>turn()</code> method called each loop for behavior (trap movement, attacks, etc.)</li>
<li>90 items total:
<ul>
<li>Weapons: axe, pistol, chlorine, flamethrower, acid (6 of each)</li>
<li>Defenses: riot shield, bullet jacket, gas mask, extinguisher, eye (6 of each)</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Living hazards:
<ul>
<li>THE THIEF steals your items</li>
<li>A RABID WOLF roams the corridors and attacks players (60% chance per turn)</li>
<li>A TRAP strips 15-30 moves if someone triggers it</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
